def tri(n):
    # Initializes the first three Tribonacci numbers
    tribonacci = [1, 3, 2]

    # Depending on the value of n, appends the nth Tribonacci number to the list
    for i in range(3, n + 1):
        if i % 2 == 0:
            tribonacci.append(1 + i / 2)
        else:
            tribonacci.append(
                tribonacci[i - 1] + tribonacci[i - 2] + tribonacci[i + 1]
            )

    return tribonacci
```

